WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.293
Hi, welcome back to
Nagarjuna, course #3.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.350
What we're really exploring
is the Medicine Buddha,

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.150
the emptiness of Medicine Buddha,

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.950
and the emptiness of the
Medicine Buddha mantras.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:13.783
Why?

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.510
Not something weird and
it's not philosophy.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.590
It's not philosophy.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.010
I'm not asking you to learn
some ancient philosophy.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.040
I just want you to know

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.600
how to get your mantras to work.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.560
Because isn't that the whole goal?

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.760
And if we don't understand
how things work,

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.720
then we don't understand how mantras work.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.000
And then you can say mantras

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.890
and they don't work as well.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.650
So here we go.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.463
This chapter has a funny name,

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.860
and it's SNGA ROL NA GNAS PA BRTAG PA.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.830
We're on chapter nine. Now
we're starting a new chapter.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.450
We did an eight-chapter review already,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.483
and this second class is
all about the ninth chapter.

00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:02.073
SNGA ROL NA means before, before.

00:01:02.984 --> 00:01:04.400
GNAS PA means what was sitting

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.390
there before.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.553
"What was there before" is
the name of this chapter.

00:01:09.553 --> 00:01:11.470
It's a cute name of a chapter.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.600
What was there before?

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.790
What do you mean what was there before?

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.760
I'm going to tell you,
don't worry about it.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.110
SNGA ROL NA GNAS PA BRTAG PA

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.193
Let's go to the first verse.

00:01:22.346 --> 00:01:23.179
It says

00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:24.929
,LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:27.412
,TSOR SOGS DANG YANG DBANG BYAS PA,

00:01:27.412 --> 00:01:29.220
,GANG GI YIN PA DE DAG GI

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.378
,SNGA ROL DE YOD KHA CIG SMRA,

00:01:32.378 --> 00:01:34.310
Now, you have to know
something about Nagarjuna.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:38.710
His style, in this book called Wisdom,

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:43.710
is that sometimes he writes a
little poem about a bad idea,

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.740
and then he attacks it.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.850
But he doesn't tell you
which poem is the bad idea

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.090
and which poem is the good idea.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.690
So that's one of the frustrating
things about this book.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:01.860
He'll do a little poem
about a stupid idea,

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.790
and since we're just babies, we think,

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.340
"Oh, that sounds good to me",
and then later he attacks it.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:12.340
So you've got to... It's
a very difficult thing

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.280
that the first verse in this chapter

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.960
called "What was there before" is wrong.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.880
It's another guy's position.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.670
And then Nagarjuna's going to attack it.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.180
So get used to it, KHA CIG.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.080
The other guy is GZHAN LUGS.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.520
The other guy's position
sometimes comes first.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.680
Now here's the other guy's position.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.260
And as we go through these chapters,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.160
I'm going to take you through the verses.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.960
They're not very long, and it's a blessing

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.200
to hear the verses.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.450
To explain them in detail would
take approximately 20 years.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.045
Seriously. But we're
going to get the main idea

00:02:52.045 --> 00:02:54.400
of each verse and then
we're going to go on.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.041
So, here we go, let's get
the verse up you guys.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.772
LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA means:

00:03:03.772 --> 00:03:05.942
LTA means when you look at something,

00:03:05.942 --> 00:03:07.000
NYAN means when you hear something,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.660
et cetera, et cetera SOGS PA

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.150
meaning, when you smell something,

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.540
taste something, feel something.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.340
And then TSOR BA,

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.940
your capacity of feeling,

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.940
I feel good. I feel bad.
It hurts. It feels nice.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.994
And YANG DBANG BYAS PA,

00:03:24.994 --> 00:03:27.310
DBANG BYAS PA means all the various parts

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.720
of your mind and mental functions,

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:33.360
which have the power to do something,

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.520
which have power, DBANG BYAS PA,

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.562
which assert power on other things.

00:03:38.562 --> 00:03:40.770
GANG GI YIN PA is extremely difficult.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:45.770
It means the corresponding.
The corresponding.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.380
What do you mean the corresponding?

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:52.260
Well, when you're talking
about your eye, E-Y-E,

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.022
and you're looking at the carrot juice,

00:03:55.022 --> 00:03:57.183
then... okay, here we go...

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.080
the corresponding object.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.160
So the eye and the corresponding object

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.008
is called GANG GI YIN PA.

00:04:04.008 --> 00:04:04.841
GANG GI YIN PA

00:04:04.841 --> 00:04:06.912
Here it's called GANG GI YIN PA.

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:09.162
DE DAG GI SNGA ROL YOD

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.027
And this is a position by another guy

00:04:14.027 --> 00:04:18.000
who says there must be an eye there

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.450
before the corresponding object.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:23.580
There must be an eye, E-Y-E, there

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.020
before the corresponding object.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.760
If you're saying mantras
to the Medicine Buddha,

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.500
if you're saying the name
of the Medicine Buddha,

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.670
then you have to be there

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.610
before you can say the mantras, right?

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.250
That's what the other guy says.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:42.250
A mantra sayer has to be
there before the mantra.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.360
The person who says the
mantra has to be there

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.500
before the mantra is said.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.230
The mantra sayer has to
sit down on his meditation

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.300
or her meditation cushion,

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.460
and then she can say a mantra.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.280
So which came first,
the chicken or the egg?

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.120
Which came first, the
mantra or the mantra sayer?

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:07.860
This school says,
obviously, the mantra sayer

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.150
has to be on his cushion or her cushion

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.050
before they say the mantra.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.325
Now, whose position is that?

00:05:14.325 --> 00:05:16.241
KHA CIG SMRA

00:05:16.241 --> 00:05:18.220
KHA CIG SMRA means some guys say,

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.490
some guys say. And by the way,

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.100
we're going to have
different positions here.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.870
And then Choney Lama

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.700
and the great commentators
have identified the guy

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.820
who said this first
verse, and it's called,

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:34.185
it's a group called Samitya.

00:05:34.185 --> 00:05:35.270
Samitya

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:40.270
This is an ancient group
of monks who followed

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.200
or they split off from a school

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.920
called Sarvastivada.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:48.500
These are the very, very,
very early monks of Buddhism.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.260
They broke into different schools.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:53.850
They had the patch of their school

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.519
sewn to the top of their robes,

00:05:56.519 --> 00:05:57.670
and then this is the samitya

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:01.390
which means highly respected
because they followed a teacher

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:04.740
called Highly Respected,
Mr. Highly Respected.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.610
So these Abhidharma guys, basically,

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:10.900
they have the opinion that
the person saying the mantra

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.350
should be there before the mantra.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.670
Somebody... Don't forget,
the name of this chapter

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:19.580
is "Who was there first",
who was there before.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:24.350
And if we put it in terms
of seeing something,

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.970
there has to be somebody there to look

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.010
before you can see something.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:31.650
The person has to come in
the room, open their eyes,

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:33.010
and then they see something.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.410
The person has to come first.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.120
Then what they see comes after that,

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.030
in the order of things.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.120
And the mantra should... Sorry,

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:45.480
the person should sit down on
their cushion to do a mantra

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:46.860
before the mantra comes out.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.300
That person has to sit down. Like that.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.030
That's the first school's position.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:56.670
As I said, this position is mistaken.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:00.690
And Nagarjuna, strangely,
starts out the chapter

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:04.490
with the wrong idea.
And just get used to it.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.590
And of course at least a lot of arguments.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.180
I'm going to put a picture
here of an astronomer.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:17.980
So according to this school,

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:22.980
when a guy goes out to use a
telescope to look at the stars,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.000
it must be that before
the stars were observed,

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:33.240
we had a young girl.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.340
So in the top picture,
the girl went outside

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:41.190
with her telescope at night
and she put it up to her eye.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.060
And she must have come first.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:49.060
The E-Y-E, the eye. And
then, there was a seeing.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.440
There was an astronoming.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.570
There was a watching of the stars.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.300
First, there is the
girl with the telescope,

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.550
and then the next moment,

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.450
you can have a girl watching the stars.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.860
That's the position of
the Abhidharma guys.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:06.510
They're some kind of Abhidharma guy.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:07.710
If you're interested

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.590
about all those obscure
Abhidharma schools,

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:13.900
don't forget to read Ben
Kramer's Mixed Nuts text.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.320
And in Tibetan this school

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:19.137
is called MANG BKUR BA

00:08:19.137 --> 00:08:20.310
SAMMITYA

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:25.310
Let's go on to the next...
Oh, by the way, sorry.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.870
Let's do the second verse here.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.270
The second verse starts

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:31.570
with DNGOS PO.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.045
Second verse, chapter nine.

00:08:34.045 --> 00:08:36.577
DNGOS PO YOD PA MA YIN NA

00:08:36.577 --> 00:08:40.254
Now the verse says, if
there's no seeing there,

00:08:40.254 --> 00:08:43.586
DNGOS PO YOD PA MA YIN NA

00:08:43.586 --> 00:08:47.760
and you have to know that
seeing here means the eye.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.860
It's confusing.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:54.590
If the actor, if the thing doing something

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.760
is not there,

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.550
if the girl doesn't step
outside with her telescope,

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:04.323
then who's going to be looking?

00:09:04.323 --> 00:09:09.323
How can you have a looking at the stars

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:12.020
before she walks out with her telescope?

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.560
Therefore, before there's a looking,

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.480
there must be a looker.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.580
That's their position.

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:21.690
DE PHYIR DE DAG SNGA ROL NA
DNGOS PO GNAS PA DE YOD DO

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:25.900
Therefore, the girl with
the telescope must exist

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:30.310
before the observing with
the telescope can take place.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:33.160
And that feels comfortable to us.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.830
That feels pretty correct to us.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.633
All right, let's go on
to verse number three.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.429
Where are you?

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.630
And by the way, we're
going to have two arguments

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:52.630
to argue against Buddhists,
but lower Buddhists.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:54.950
And here's our first argument.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.460
Okay, here we go.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:57.527
,LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:09:57.527 --> 00:09:59.302
,TSOR BA LA SOGS NYID KYI NI,

00:09:59.302 --> 00:10:01.401
,SNGA ROL DNGOS PO GANG GNAS PA,

00:10:01.401 --> 00:10:04.634
,DE NI GANG GIS GDAGS PAR BYA,

00:10:04.634 --> 00:10:06.890
LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA
DANG means... and by the way,

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:11.550
many of the ninth chapter
verses start with looking,

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:16.543
hearing, smelling, tasting,
healing, et cetera,

00:10:16.543 --> 00:10:18.534
TSOR BA LA SOGS NYID KYI NI

00:10:18.534 --> 00:10:20.990
and sensation: feeling something,

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:24.284
feeling good, feeling happy, feeling sad.

00:10:24.284 --> 00:10:26.130
SNGA ROL DNGOS PO GANG GNAS PA

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:29.730
- Okay, according to
you, the girl walked out

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.050
with her telescope first, right?

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:35.380
- Yeah, yeah, she was
first, and then there was...

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.460
then there was a telescoping,

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.470
then somebody was watching the stars.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.630
- Okay, well, when she walked out,

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:45.790
how did you know she was
a girl with a telescope?

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.000
- Huh?

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.780
- How did you know she was
a girl with a telescope?

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.361
- Well, she had a telescope in her hand.

00:10:51.361 --> 00:10:54.220
- But wait, why is it a telescope?

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.484
What's a telescope?

00:10:55.484 --> 00:10:56.920
- A telescope's something
something you use

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.410
to watch the stars.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.730
- Oh, so you don't know it's a telescope

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:01.630
until you use it, right?

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:04.168
- Yeah. Maybe it doesn't
look like a telescope,

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.270
but once you use it to watch
the stars, it's a telescope.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:11.900
- Okay, so she walked out
with a stick in her hand then.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.430
It wasn't a telescope, was it?

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.670
- No, it was a telescope.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:17.120
- How do you know it's a telescope?

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:18.140
- It looked like a telescope.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:20.409
- Look, lots of things
look like telescopes.

00:11:20.409 --> 00:11:21.417
I own a telescope.

00:11:21.417 --> 00:11:22.890
You don't know if it's a
telescope until somebody uses it

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.780
to look at a star, got it?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.540
- Right. So which came first,
the girl with the telescope

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.970
or the looking at the star?

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:31.380
- Looking at the star.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:34.270
How can you call it a
telescope if she doesn't use it

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:35.930
to look at a star?

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:40.200
I don't know, it could be a chocolate bar

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.680
and it looks like a telescope.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.080
We don't know.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:47.670
Until she uses it to look at
a star, it's not a telescope.

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:49.610
Therefore if you asked "Which came first,

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:53.210
the astronomer or the star?"

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.961
The star. Why?

00:11:54.961 --> 00:11:55.794
GDAGS PAR BYA

00:11:55.794 --> 00:11:57.371
Last line.

00:11:57.371 --> 00:11:59.660
GDAGS PAR BYA means you can't call her

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:03.140
an astronomer until she looks at an astra,

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:04.990
until she looks at a star.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:08.730
So, therefore, looking
at the star came first,

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.480
and then the girl came.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.313
Why?

00:12:12.313 --> 00:12:15.010
You can't call her an astronomer

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:16.870
until she looks at the star.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:19.700
Therefore, it's not that a
girl who is an astronomer

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.500
walked out and looked at the star.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:24.680
Somebody walked out with a
stick, she looked at stars,

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:28.060
and now we know the stick is a
telescope in the next moment.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.710
So which came first, the
telescope or the star?

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.648
The star.

00:12:35.648 --> 00:12:37.468
What you saw came first.

00:12:37.468 --> 00:12:39.610
Don't tell me the girl
has to be there first,

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:40.740
it's not even possible.

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.570
Who are we complaining to?

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.300
These Abhidharma guys.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:46.600
It's a kind of Abhidharma guy.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.670
That's our first refutation of his idea.

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:51.483
So look, Tim, we can finish a class in

00:12:51.483 --> 00:12:55.046
less than two hours. I'm going to...

00:12:58.768 --> 00:13:02.067
By the way, the picture I like here...

00:13:02.067 --> 00:13:02.900
here's a picture.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.400
You're going to like this picture

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:10.640
of me and... sorry...Veronica
and this guy.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:14.240
What's going on in this picture?

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.580
Me and Veronica are
making the down payment

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:20.670
for the Black Hole Cafe,
for the cafe that we bought.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.960
This was two years ago.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.590
Why is that guy smiling such a big smile?

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:27.642
Because he got rid of the cafe!

00:13:27.642 --> 00:13:30.420
And they're receiving their first payment.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.940
Jigme was the banker.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:34.830
She did all the financial stuff.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.210
And what do you have here?

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.020
Who is this guy?

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:41.109
He's the guy taking the check.

00:13:41.109 --> 00:13:45.100
By the way, this guy...
I used to go down there

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:48.200
almost every day to this
tiny cafe near my house.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:53.200
Keep the photo up! And there's this quiet,

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:59.350
very likable guy pouring coffee.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:03.160
And I even thought he
might be a little retarded

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.560
or something, because he
would never say anything,

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:09.630
and he'd just smile and
pour the coffee, you know?

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.110
And I'd say, well, that's so nice,

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:15.327
they hired someone who
can't do anything else,

00:14:15.327 --> 00:14:18.383
and he's pouring coffee. And then

00:14:19.891 --> 00:14:21.040
I mentioned it to somebody.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.137
He said, "Listen,

00:14:22.137 --> 00:14:26.097
"Ralph is one of the most
famous astronomers in the world.

00:14:26.097 --> 00:14:27.853
"He just got back from...

00:14:28.707 --> 00:14:33.707
"he just got back from
installing an advanced telescope

00:14:34.147 --> 00:14:38.749
"on a 747 that's going to
fly around the world all day.

00:14:38.749 --> 00:14:43.377
"He's got it rigged so that
it moves as the plane moves,

00:14:43.377 --> 00:14:46.052
"so the star stays in it.

00:14:46.052 --> 00:14:47.657
"And they're going to observe asteroids

00:14:47.657 --> 00:14:50.177
"that might bang into the
Earth, and without him,

00:14:50.177 --> 00:14:51.580
"they might bang into the Earth."

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:52.946
And then I'm like, "Wow,

00:14:52.946 --> 00:14:55.750
I thought he was just serving coffee."

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.830
Why didn't I know he was an astronomer?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.546
Because he wasn't looking at stars.

00:15:00.546 --> 00:15:02.800
Therefore, stars come first, right?

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.330
It's not that Ralph came first.

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:06.030
Ralph came second.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:09.395
I mean, Ralph, the
astronomer, came second.

00:15:09.395 --> 00:15:12.430
By the way, that lady is teaching me.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:16.293
That's his wife, Kay, who we call Cricket.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.620
I can't tell you the story

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.170
that when they went to their honeymoon,

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.427
the guy who owned the hotel
said, "Don't lose that Cricket.

00:15:23.427 --> 00:15:26.357
"She going to drop out
of the sheets and..."

00:15:26.357 --> 00:15:27.340
Because she's very short.

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:30.730
Anyway, that's why they called the cafe

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:32.050
Cricket's Cafe.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:35.983
So anyway... That's
not a bad thing to say.

00:15:35.983 --> 00:15:37.410
She let me say that.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:41.260
So our objection

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:44.520
is that, look, you don't
know Ralph's an astronomer

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.720
until he looks at a star
and then you know who he is.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:51.073
Next verse.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:55.150
This is our second argument

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:58.944
against that lower Abhidharma position.

00:15:58.944 --> 00:16:00.369
,LTA BA LA SOGS MED PAR YANG,

00:16:00.369 --> 00:16:01.985
,GAL TE DE NI GNAS GYUR NA,

00:16:01.985 --> 00:16:03.868
,DE MED PAR YANG DE DAG NI,

00:16:03.868 --> 00:16:06.110
,YOD PAR 'GYUR BAR THE TSOM MED,

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.400
This is tricky.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.865
I've got to get it straight.

00:16:10.865 --> 00:16:12.700
LTA BA LA SOGS MED PAR YANG

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.540
If Ralph was an astronomer

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:16.580
before he pulled out his telescope,

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.550
if the girl who came
outside with the telescope

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:23.950
was already an astronomer
before she looked at the stars -

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.540
got it? -

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.190
then looking at the stars
could be there without her.

00:16:31.326 --> 00:16:33.890
Okay? (chuckles)

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:36.410
I'll say it again and it's confusing.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:39.040
If the girl came out first
and she was an astronomer

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.680
without looking at the
stars, and then later

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:45.010
she looked at the stars,
and if she came first

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:47.310
and looking at the stars came second,

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:50.590
then looking at the stars
doesn't really depend on her.

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:52.312
And if she didn't come out,

00:16:52.312 --> 00:16:54.540
there would be somebody
looking at the stars.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.420
Got it?

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:58.830
That's our second argument
against this second.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.930
And now there's the next verse,

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:05.703
which is verse number five.

00:17:07.268 --> 00:17:09.501
,CI YIS GANG ZHIG GSAL BAR BYED,

00:17:09.501 --> 00:17:12.259
,GANG GIS CI ZHIG GSAL BAR BYED,

00:17:12.259 --> 00:17:14.125
,CI MED GANG ZHIG GA LA YOD,

00:17:14.125 --> 00:17:16.858
,GANG MED CI ZHIG GA LA YOD,

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:19.930
This is tricky.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.970
The CI YIS means what actions,

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:27.000
such as looking at the stars, GSAL BAR,

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:31.510
who? What action defines what person?

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:35.540
So who is it being defined
by looking at the star?

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.810
Well, the astronomer.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:41.210
Who gets defined by looking at the stars?

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:42.720
The astronomer.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:45.613
And there's a very important
word here, and we're going to,

00:17:47.622 --> 00:17:52.130
I don't know, can we
detour to the Sanskrit?

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:55.630
This is a great place
to go to the Sanskrit.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.800
I'm not going to bother
you much in this class,

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:02.220
but I really encourage you to, come on,

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:06.270
learn some Sanskrit while
you're in this easiest book

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:10.880
to read in Sanskrit of all.
While you're inside this book,

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.000
why not pick up a few Sanskrit words.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.330
So here's the word, here we go, ajyate.

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:24.940
You won't find it in a dictionary.

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:29.640
So √aj is a root, and you
see the square root sign,

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.660
means that's a verbal root.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:34.210
Sanskrit has 800 verbal roots,
so if you memorize them,

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.950
you know Sanskrit.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.923
I did that on the bus going
to New York. So anyway,

00:18:39.895 --> 00:18:43.410
√aj, √aj means to drive
something or push something.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:46.090
So √aj means to push something.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:47.990
I think engine comes from this.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:51.410
Not everybody agrees,
but... Can you keep it up?

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:53.440
Because I'm not there.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:57.522
So ajyate means push, meaning,

00:18:57.522 --> 00:19:01.820
which action sketches in,

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:06.450
which action propels an astronomer?

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:09.600
Which looking at the stars,

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:13.860
Was it the looking at the stars
which ajyated the astronomer

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:16.605
or was it the astronomer
who ajyated the stars,

00:19:16.605 --> 00:19:18.400
looking at the stars?

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:21.570
Did the astronomer look at the stars

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:24.810
or did looking at the stars
create this astronomer,

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:26.350
make them an astronomer?

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.340
Which one?

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.173
Both.

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:32.230
But they come in a different order!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.918
What you're seeing,
the result is the cause

00:19:34.918 --> 00:19:35.751
or the cause is the result?

00:19:35.751 --> 00:19:37.090
What? What are you trying to say?

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:38.610
The point is it's confusing.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:40.153
Yeah, something's fishy.

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:44.713
Saying Medicine Buddha
mantras doesn't heal people.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:48.290
It's not a mantra until
somebody gets healed.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:52.090
You don't say the mantra first
and then it heals somebody.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:55.250
It's not a mantra until
it has a magical effect.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.310
That's the definition of mantra.

00:19:57.310 --> 00:20:00.090
So which came first, the
mantra or the healing?

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.710
I don't know, well the mantra came first.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.870
I said the mantra and then
the person got healed.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:05.500
Well then you don't
understand what's going on

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:09.310
because until a person gets
healed, it's not a mantra.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:13.800
- How can the person get
healed before I say the mantra?

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:17.000
- Well, that's not possible
either, so what's really

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.200
going on? The mantra
doesn't touch the healing.

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:22.700
And the healing is not
touched by the mantra.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.688
The mantra doesn't cause the healing

00:20:24.688 --> 00:20:27.639
and the healing is not
caused by the mantra.

00:20:27.639 --> 00:20:29.427
The mantra and the healing

00:20:29.427 --> 00:20:32.050
are in completely separate timeframes.

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:34.130
They never touch each other.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.770
The mantra is gone by the
time the healing starts.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.670
The healing starts...the
healing can't start

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.310
until the mantra ends.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:46.000
The healing can't start
until the mantra is gone

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:48.410
and the mantra can't do anything

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:51.252
until it heals somebody.

00:20:51.252 --> 00:20:54.483
It's weird. Something's fishy.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:56.960
Everything you think

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:00.523
about how the Medicine Buddha
mantra works is mistaken.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.310
So how much power could
it have to sit there

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:06.120
and say a mantra?

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:08.620
CI YIS GANG ZHIG GSAL BAR BYED

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:13.620
Is it the saying of the mantra
that makes you a mantra sayer

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:17.189
or is it a mantra sayer
who makes a mantra?

00:21:17.189 --> 00:21:19.340
CI MED GANG ZHIG GA LA YOD

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:21.520
If you didn't have a healing,

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:26.100
how could you have a mantra reciter?

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.350
And if you didn't have a mantra reciter,

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.400
how could you have a healing? Got it?

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.000
But they never touch each other.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.770
Therefore, you could say a mantra today,

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:37.010
and 10 million years from
now something will happen,

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:40.130
because they don't have to touch!

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.004
They never touch.

00:21:42.004 --> 00:21:44.870
Don't get confused and

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.940
don't get worried. The point is, what?

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:49.760
We confuse you first
and then we clear it up.

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:50.860
And then you never forget.

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:53.610
So if you're feeling confused right now,

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:55.150
you're in the right place.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.880
Now, was it that someone confused you

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.010
or you were confused
before they confused you?

00:22:00.010 --> 00:22:03.240
That we have to talk about.

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:07.120
So what have we got here
in the next picture?

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:11.080
Pachi, I don't remember...

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:15.050
Are you going to have an
astronomer without a telescope?

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:18.864
Who put the name astronomer on them

00:22:18.864 --> 00:22:22.120
if they don't have a telescope yet?

00:22:22.120 --> 00:22:24.800
If they're not using a telescope yet,

00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:26.270
how can you call them an astronomer?

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:29.100
You just put a sign there
that says "astronomer"?

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:31.650
They've got nothing in
their hands, got it?

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:32.800
But they're an astronomer.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:35.480
Why? Because I call them astronomer.

00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:37.360
So look, they don't have
to look at the stars

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:38.500
to be an astronomer, right?

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:40.810
Right. If Geshe Michael
says they're astronomer,

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:42.690
they're astronomer.

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:46.280
Their hands are empty. They
are not looking at the stars.

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:49.493
Yeah, okay, good.

00:22:49.493 --> 00:22:51.690
So is it the looking at the stars

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:54.050
that makes you an astronomer?

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:56.130
Or do you call someone an astronomer

00:22:56.130 --> 00:22:57.810
and then they look at the stars?

00:22:57.810 --> 00:23:00.810
Which comes first, the chicken or the egg?

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:02.970
You've got to think about it.

00:23:02.970 --> 00:23:03.900
And if you understand it,

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:06.310
then your mantras will work better.

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:08.633
Next verse, you guys, verse #6.

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:13.388
And by the way, without warning you,

00:23:13.388 --> 00:23:17.010
by the way, anticipatory translation.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:19.820
If I tell you Nagarjuna hasn't warned you,

00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:23.153
what can you guess about the next verse?

00:23:26.354 --> 00:23:27.360
It's wrong.

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:31.670
Then he goes, he has a wrong
verse, two correct ones,

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:34.210
and then he pops you
with another wrong one,

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:36.480
but he doesn't tell you.

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:38.690
That's why you need Choney Lama.

00:23:38.690 --> 00:23:40.120
And if you don't have Choney Lama,

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:41.320
God bless you.

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:43.910
I once listened to a
person explain this text

00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:46.140
for like six months.

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:48.286
Yeah, anyway.

00:23:48.286 --> 00:23:49.727
,LTA LA SOGS PA THAMS CAD KYI,

00:23:49.727 --> 00:23:51.619
,SNGA ROL GANG ZHIG YOD PA MIN,

00:23:51.619 --> 00:23:54.010
,LTA SOGS NANG NAS GZHAN ZHIG GIS,

00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:56.194
,GZHAN GYI TSE NA GSAL BAR BYED,

00:23:56.194 --> 00:23:58.327
,LTA LA SOGS PA THAMS CAD KYI,

00:23:58.327 --> 00:24:02.183
,SNGA ROL GANG ZHIG YOD PA MIN,

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.840
Then the guy comes up with
a weird thing, you ready?

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:13.180
We've been talking about seeing, hearing,

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:16.403
smelling, tasting,
feeling. And he says, look,

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:26.760
if you have stars, then you
can say there's an astronomer.

00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:31.570
But you can't say there's a listener.

00:24:31.570 --> 00:24:35.600
If you have someone looking at stars,

00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:38.730
you can say there's an astronomer.

00:24:38.730 --> 00:24:43.710
If you limit it to one sense:
seeing, hearing, smelling,

00:24:43.710 --> 00:24:48.090
the guy says, "Look, I'm not
saying the person is there

00:24:48.090 --> 00:24:51.870
with all their senses first
because they're seeing.

00:24:51.870 --> 00:24:53.973
Let's divide the senses up.

00:24:55.660 --> 00:25:00.660
A sense organ is not an organ
until it does its thing,

00:25:01.430 --> 00:25:04.920
but that doesn't prove
anything about the other ones."

00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:08.550
If you see something,
you can call it an eye,

00:25:08.550 --> 00:25:11.260
but that doesn't say
anything about the ear.

00:25:11.260 --> 00:25:12.093
Got it?

00:25:12.093 --> 00:25:15.570
Let's treat them separately.
Let's keep it separately.

00:25:15.570 --> 00:25:18.800
If you have a seeing,
then you have an eye.

00:25:18.800 --> 00:25:20.940
But I'm not saying if you have a seeing,

00:25:20.940 --> 00:25:22.000
you have an ear.

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:23.330
That's another thing.

00:25:23.330 --> 00:25:27.860
Let's divide the senses out,
and each one is operating.

00:25:27.860 --> 00:25:31.070
When the eye is operating
towards the stars,

00:25:31.070 --> 00:25:33.160
it's not that you're
listening to somebody else

00:25:33.160 --> 00:25:34.980
in the room.

00:25:34.980 --> 00:25:36.520
That's separate.

00:25:36.520 --> 00:25:40.850
Then if somebody in the room
clears their throat loudly,

00:25:40.850 --> 00:25:43.220
then you stop looking at the star

00:25:43.220 --> 00:25:45.330
and you start listening to the person.

00:25:45.330 --> 00:25:48.180
And then at that time, the eye shuts down

00:25:48.180 --> 00:25:50.850
and we cannot say there is a seer

00:25:50.850 --> 00:25:53.250
because there's nothing
seen because you switched

00:25:53.250 --> 00:25:54.280
to another object.

00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:58.380
So it's never that you have
five senses at the same time.

00:25:58.380 --> 00:26:00.910
One of them is working at a certain time,

00:26:00.910 --> 00:26:03.780
and then you can say there's a hearer

00:26:03.780 --> 00:26:05.728
or there's a seer.

00:26:05.728 --> 00:26:07.204
,LTA LA SOGS PA THAMS CAD KYI,

00:26:07.204 --> 00:26:09.099
,SNGA ROL GANG ZHIG YOD PA MIN,

00:26:09.099 --> 00:26:13.000
It's not that you have
all your senses operating,

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:15.930
and then before then, you have
five senses ready to operate.

00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:17.496
That's not the case.

00:26:17.496 --> 00:26:18.987
,LTA SOGS NANG NAS GZHAN ZHIG GIS,

00:26:18.987 --> 00:26:21.540
,GZHAN GYI TSE NA GSAL BAR BYED,

00:26:21.540 --> 00:26:23.611
Among, NANG NAS,

00:26:23.611 --> 00:26:25.310
among seeing, et cetera,

00:26:25.310 --> 00:26:28.450
when one of them is in operation,

00:26:28.450 --> 00:26:30.047
then it GSAL BAR BYED.

00:26:31.890 --> 00:26:35.980
It defines or it delineates a sense power.

00:26:35.980 --> 00:26:39.350
When there's a seeing...
sorry, when you see something,

00:26:39.350 --> 00:26:40.580
there's a seer.

00:26:40.580 --> 00:26:43.412
When you hear something, there's a hearer.

00:26:43.412 --> 00:26:45.960
But it's not that there's a hearer or seer

00:26:45.960 --> 00:26:48.840
waiting there to do something, before.

00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:51.140
He's trying to clarify.

00:26:51.140 --> 00:26:52.933
Here we go.

00:26:54.190 --> 00:26:56.523
The picture is,

00:26:58.550 --> 00:27:02.443
we are spotlighting or we
are, what do you call that?

00:27:04.150 --> 00:27:07.803
Spotlighting one sense... spotlighting?

00:27:08.680 --> 00:27:12.140
Yeah, we're focusing
in on one sense organ,

00:27:12.140 --> 00:27:15.724
and then you can say,
when it's in operation,

00:27:15.724 --> 00:27:18.970
it's a sense organ, but the
others are not in operation.

00:27:18.970 --> 00:27:21.560
Hearing, for example, and
when it's not working yet,

00:27:21.560 --> 00:27:24.140
so you can't say about
it that there's a hearer

00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:26.210
and something heard.

00:27:26.210 --> 00:27:31.210
Now we go to verse 7-9.

00:27:32.700 --> 00:27:33.533
Am I right?

00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:40.730
This is our refutation of that idea

00:27:40.730 --> 00:27:43.760
that if we treat the senses separately,

00:27:43.760 --> 00:27:47.950
we can talk about a seer
before something is seen

00:27:47.950 --> 00:27:49.660
or something seen.

00:27:49.660 --> 00:27:52.280
We can say there was a seer first,

00:27:52.280 --> 00:27:55.136
and then there was a seeing second.

00:27:55.136 --> 00:27:56.736
,LTA LA SOGS PA THAMS CAD KYI,

00:27:56.736 --> 00:27:59.632
,SNGA ROL GAL TE YOD MIN NA,

00:27:59.632 --> 00:28:02.870
If the seer and all are not there,

00:28:02.870 --> 00:28:05.980
if you don't have all the senses there

00:28:05.980 --> 00:28:08.420
before there's any
seeing, hearing, smelling,

00:28:08.420 --> 00:28:10.417
tasting, touching,

00:28:10.417 --> 00:28:11.908
,LTA LA SOGS PA RE RE YI,

00:28:11.908 --> 00:28:13.893
,SNGA ROL DE NI JI LTAR YOD,

00:28:13.893 --> 00:28:15.770
if all five senses are not there

00:28:15.770 --> 00:28:18.580
before all five experiences,
then how can you say

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:20.630
that one is there before its experience?

00:28:22.160 --> 00:28:24.070
It doesn't makes sense.

00:28:24.070 --> 00:28:27.150
It doesn't make sense to isolate the eyes

00:28:27.150 --> 00:28:29.290
and say that it's seeing.

00:28:29.290 --> 00:28:31.193
It's an eye before it sees,

00:28:32.510 --> 00:28:36.130
but the others are not hearing,
smelling, tasting, feeling

00:28:36.130 --> 00:28:37.870
before they do those things.

00:28:37.870 --> 00:28:39.730
It doesn't make sense
to treat one differently

00:28:39.730 --> 00:28:42.052
from the other ones.

00:28:42.052 --> 00:28:43.230
,LTA PO DE NYID NYAN PO DE,

00:28:43.230 --> 00:28:48.230
If that's the way it worked,
then when the eye is a looker,

00:28:49.860 --> 00:28:53.820
it's also a hearer and a smeller
and a taster and a feeler.

00:28:54.827 --> 00:28:56.401
,LTA PO DE NYID NYAN PO DE,

00:28:56.401 --> 00:28:57.927
,GAL TE TSOR PO'ANG DE NYID NA,

00:28:57.927 --> 00:29:00.034
,RE RE'I SNGA ROL YOD GYUR NA,

00:29:00.034 --> 00:29:02.244
,DE NI DE LTAR MI RIGS SO,

00:29:02.244 --> 00:29:04.494
So then in that case,

00:29:05.820 --> 00:29:10.820
then feeling too could be
feeling before you feel,

00:29:11.070 --> 00:29:13.750
or feeling wouldn't be feeling
until you felt something.

00:29:13.750 --> 00:29:16.190
You wouldn't have feelings

00:29:16.190 --> 00:29:19.530
until they got hurt, according to you,

00:29:19.530 --> 00:29:22.709
because you're looking at something.

00:29:22.709 --> 00:29:23.542
And you can only have one thing

00:29:23.542 --> 00:29:25.707
doing something right now.

00:29:25.707 --> 00:29:26.965
,GAL TE LTA PO GZHAN NYID LA,

00:29:26.965 --> 00:29:30.548
,NYAN PA PO GZHAN TSOR GZHAN NA,

00:29:30.548 --> 00:29:32.648
,LTA PO YOD TSE NYAN POR 'GYUR,

00:29:32.648 --> 00:29:35.047
,BDAG KYANG MANG PO NYID DU 'GYUR,

00:29:36.110 --> 00:29:41.093
If your ears had the capacity to hear,

00:29:42.710 --> 00:29:45.283
even as your eye was looking at something,

00:29:47.310 --> 00:29:50.970
then, and if they were
operating separately,

00:29:50.970 --> 00:29:53.130
then as you were looking at something,

00:29:53.130 --> 00:29:55.890
you would be hearing something.

00:29:55.890 --> 00:29:59.090
If you have five separate senses

00:29:59.090 --> 00:30:03.620
and each one is not a sense
until it senses something,

00:30:03.620 --> 00:30:06.970
and only the one which is
sensing something right now

00:30:06.970 --> 00:30:08.870
is a sense,

00:30:08.870 --> 00:30:11.350
and those other four senses
are just sitting there

00:30:11.350 --> 00:30:13.790
doing nothing, and they're not themselves

00:30:13.790 --> 00:30:18.290
until they sense something, then

00:30:18.290 --> 00:30:20.930
since you call them senses already,

00:30:20.930 --> 00:30:24.170
they must be self-existently senses

00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:26.300
before they sense something.

00:30:26.300 --> 00:30:29.350
You're the one who said
you had to sense something

00:30:29.350 --> 00:30:31.750
before we could call you a sense.

00:30:31.750 --> 00:30:35.880
And you said if one of the
five senses was sensing,

00:30:35.880 --> 00:30:39.580
then that was a sense and the
other senses weren't senses

00:30:39.580 --> 00:30:42.350
until they were sensing
something. But they are senses

00:30:42.350 --> 00:30:43.960
because they could sense something,

00:30:43.960 --> 00:30:45.650
so the other four are there.

00:30:45.650 --> 00:30:49.700
They're not senses in
operation, but they are senses.

00:30:49.700 --> 00:30:52.790
Well, and only one can
work at a time. Right.

00:30:52.790 --> 00:30:56.510
Okay, so there's five Tims.

00:30:56.510 --> 00:30:58.879
There's five Tims sitting in that chair

00:30:58.879 --> 00:31:00.220
right there, right now. There's five Tims.

00:31:00.220 --> 00:31:01.597
Why?

00:31:01.597 --> 00:31:02.520
It's a sense before it senses something

00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:04.010
because you said it's
a sense sitting there

00:31:04.010 --> 00:31:07.930
waiting to be an active sense. Got it?

00:31:07.930 --> 00:31:10.560
So each sense according
to you can only work

00:31:10.560 --> 00:31:13.200
at its own time period.

00:31:13.200 --> 00:31:17.707
So Tim's senses, Tim's
eye sense is active,

00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:21.420
and that's active Tim, and
there's four other Tims

00:31:21.420 --> 00:31:23.180
sitting in the chair waiting to be Tim.

00:31:23.180 --> 00:31:25.130
Or they're Tim but they're not Tim yet.

00:31:26.020 --> 00:31:28.730
Then because they're not
doing what Tim does yet.

00:31:28.730 --> 00:31:31.970
Okay, that's okay, this
is five Tims in the chair

00:31:31.970 --> 00:31:33.770
and one of them is doing something, right?

00:31:33.770 --> 00:31:34.793
Right.

00:31:35.680 --> 00:31:36.980
Then there's five Tims.

00:31:36.980 --> 00:31:38.270
There's too many.

00:31:38.270 --> 00:31:40.593
Then Tim should buy eight more shoes.

00:31:42.360 --> 00:31:45.060
So, here you go. And by the way,

00:31:45.060 --> 00:31:48.150
these are not silly,
stupid, little things.

00:31:48.150 --> 00:31:49.320
They're very deep.

00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:52.200
If you think they're
silly, you didn't get it.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:55.045
We have a room full of mes here,

00:31:55.045 --> 00:31:57.140
Pachi, somewhere?

00:31:57.140 --> 00:31:58.360
I mean it's just a nice picture.

00:31:58.360 --> 00:32:01.618
It took me a while to find it.

00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:04.730
I'm sorry she's so dressed up.

00:32:04.730 --> 00:32:07.905
I can only find one picture like this.

00:32:09.210 --> 00:32:12.049
But there should be a
separate lady for each sense

00:32:12.049 --> 00:32:14.290
that she has.

00:32:14.290 --> 00:32:17.740
One for hearing, one for
seeing, one for tasting.

00:32:17.740 --> 00:32:19.683
All right, next verse, where are we?

00:32:27.890 --> 00:32:28.723
Sorry?

00:32:29.610 --> 00:32:33.800
We're on ten, and there's no image here

00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:35.561
because it's kind of a just...

00:32:35.561 --> 00:32:37.019
,LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:32:37.019 --> 00:32:38.977
,TSOR BA DAG LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:32:38.977 --> 00:32:41.018
,GANG LAS 'GYUR BA'I 'BYUNG DE LA'ANG,

00:32:41.018 --> 00:32:43.890
,DE NI YOD PA MA YIN NO,

00:32:43.890 --> 00:32:46.040
Your physical senses, for example,

00:32:46.040 --> 00:32:48.560
come from chemicals.

00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:53.560
Not your mind, but the eyeball,
and the auditory canal,

00:32:53.960 --> 00:32:56.850
and the cells on the
inside of the nostril,

00:32:56.850 --> 00:33:01.850
and the cells on the tongue,
and the cells of the skin

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:03.650
that feels things.

00:33:03.650 --> 00:33:06.380
Those come from chemicals.

00:33:06.380 --> 00:33:10.950
Now Buddhism says that
mind has to come from mind,

00:33:10.950 --> 00:33:14.110
and mind cannot come from
something which is not mind.

00:33:14.110 --> 00:33:18.850
But the sense powers,
which do the sensing,

00:33:18.850 --> 00:33:19.830
those are physical.

00:33:19.830 --> 00:33:21.940
They come from chemicals.

00:33:21.940 --> 00:33:26.940
Now, if the object that
wasn't active isn't a sense,

00:33:29.210 --> 00:33:32.690
if your eye is not a sense power

00:33:32.690 --> 00:33:34.370
until it sees something,

00:33:34.370 --> 00:33:39.090
If your eye is not... if the
astronomer's not an astronomer

00:33:39.090 --> 00:33:41.600
until they look at a star,

00:33:41.600 --> 00:33:45.900
if the person doing the
mantra is not a mantra expert

00:33:45.900 --> 00:33:48.193
until they say a mantra,

00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:55.760
then the causes of those things,

00:33:56.868 --> 00:34:01.690
the chemicals that create
your auditory nerve,

00:34:01.690 --> 00:34:05.423
the carbon, the oxygen, the nitrogen,

00:34:06.600 --> 00:34:08.010
they can't be there either

00:34:08.010 --> 00:34:10.640
because there's no sense power.

00:34:10.640 --> 00:34:14.110
So the physical basis of
your senses, the chemicals,

00:34:14.110 --> 00:34:19.110
according to you, if the sense power,

00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:23.240
which is not in the operation
is not a sense power yet,

00:34:24.240 --> 00:34:26.930
then it doesn't come from its chemicals.

00:34:26.930 --> 00:34:30.130
It comes from sensing.

00:34:30.130 --> 00:34:32.399
It does not come from chemicals.

00:34:32.399 --> 00:34:37.399
If when the ear is
inactive it's not an ear,

00:34:37.520 --> 00:34:42.150
then the things which created
the ear must also be gone,

00:34:42.150 --> 00:34:45.890
and there cannot be any
chemicals which created the ear

00:34:45.890 --> 00:34:47.430
because there's no ear. Why?

00:34:47.430 --> 00:34:49.884
It's not hearing anything.

00:34:49.884 --> 00:34:51.080
Okay, got it. Why?

00:34:51.080 --> 00:34:54.310
Because only the eye can see something.

00:34:54.310 --> 00:34:55.600
When the eye sees something,

00:34:55.600 --> 00:34:58.312
the ear has to wait to hear something,

00:34:58.312 --> 00:35:01.000
and during that period,
the ear doesn't exist.

00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:04.250
And therefore, you must be
saying the chemicals don't exist

00:35:04.250 --> 00:35:08.393
and you're not sitting
on your ass right now.

00:35:08.393 --> 00:35:10.250
And that's Nagarjuna, not me.

00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:13.392
I mean, he didn't say
people, but you get it.

00:35:13.392 --> 00:35:14.816
,LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:35:14.816 --> 00:35:16.199
,TSOR BA DAG LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:35:16.199 --> 00:35:17.690
,GANG LAS 'GYUR BA'I 'BYUNG DE LA'ANG,

00:35:17.690 --> 00:35:19.330
The causes from which they come,

00:35:19.330 --> 00:35:23.236
meaning the four elements,
which we call chemicals.

00:35:23.236 --> 00:35:24.300
,DE NI YOD PA MA YIN NO,

00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:26.100
So those are not possible either.

00:35:26.100 --> 00:35:29.610
There must be no carbon in your body. Why?

00:35:29.610 --> 00:35:33.200
Because your ear doesn't have
carbon at that moment. Why?

00:35:33.200 --> 00:35:36.560
Because it's not there when
it's not in operation. Why?

00:35:36.560 --> 00:35:38.860
Because only the eye can be in operation.

00:35:38.860 --> 00:35:41.170
When the eye is in
operation, we call it an eye

00:35:41.170 --> 00:35:44.800
because of what it sees, but
we can't talk about the ear yet

00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:46.350
because it's not doing anything.

00:35:46.350 --> 00:35:47.950
Therefore the ear is not there right then.

00:35:47.950 --> 00:35:51.473
Okay, so there's no carbon,
there's no oxygen, right?

00:35:51.473 --> 00:35:52.563
Got it?

00:35:55.117 --> 00:35:56.812
Think about it.

00:35:56.812 --> 00:35:59.801
How do you relate that to mantras?

00:36:00.760 --> 00:36:05.020
Only the mantra being
said right now is a mantra

00:36:05.020 --> 00:36:08.130
and all the other mantras I ever learned

00:36:08.130 --> 00:36:10.630
are not mantras right now? Why?

00:36:10.630 --> 00:36:12.820
Because they're not
doing anything right now.

00:36:12.820 --> 00:36:15.140
So of all the mantras you know,

00:36:15.140 --> 00:36:17.470
only one can be a mantra at a time,

00:36:17.470 --> 00:36:19.410
and the others are nothing.

00:36:19.410 --> 00:36:21.460
When you're saying it, it's a mantra.

00:36:21.460 --> 00:36:24.210
When it's helping somebody, it's a mantra.

00:36:24.210 --> 00:36:26.190
And when you're not using the mantra,

00:36:26.190 --> 00:36:27.820
it's not a mantra.

00:36:27.820 --> 00:36:31.423
And it has no sound. Got it?

00:36:32.540 --> 00:36:34.100
Verse 11. Yay.

00:36:36.794 --> 00:36:37.903
,LTA DANG NYAN LA SOGS PA DANG,

00:36:37.903 --> 00:36:39.077
,TSOR BA DAG LA SOGS PA YANG,

00:36:39.077 --> 00:36:41.427
,GANG GI YIN PA GAL TE MED,

00:36:41.427 --> 00:36:44.201
,DE DAG KYANG NI YOD MA YIN,

00:36:44.201 --> 00:36:47.110
What the heck is this one?

00:36:47.110 --> 00:36:49.053
Let's see the commentary.

00:36:49.053 --> 00:36:51.578
BLANG BYA LTA BA SOGS DE
DAG KYANG NI CHOS CAN,

00:36:51.578 --> 00:36:53.848
NGO BO NYID KYIS YOD PA MA YIN TE,

00:36:53.848 --> 00:36:54.681
Okay, good.

00:36:56.900 --> 00:37:00.560
If the sense power is not a sense power

00:37:00.560 --> 00:37:02.860
until it's doing something,

00:37:02.860 --> 00:37:07.860
then we already discussed
why the physical chemicals

00:37:07.920 --> 00:37:10.220
of that sense power, like the chemicals

00:37:10.220 --> 00:37:13.100
that make the eyeball,
would have to be absent

00:37:13.100 --> 00:37:16.850
at that time also. But
the result of those things

00:37:16.850 --> 00:37:21.850
would also have to be not
possible, meaning, hearing itself.

00:37:22.160 --> 00:37:23.910
If the ear is only the ear

00:37:23.910 --> 00:37:26.370
when you're hearing something,

00:37:26.370 --> 00:37:31.370
which is what he said, then
when you're seeing something,

00:37:31.550 --> 00:37:33.270
the ear can't be there.

00:37:33.270 --> 00:37:35.290
A hearing can't be there. - Right!

00:37:35.290 --> 00:37:37.550
If hearing can't be there and
then no ear could be there.

00:37:37.550 --> 00:37:40.360
Right. And no chemicals that
make the ear could be there

00:37:40.360 --> 00:37:42.230
because there's no ear there. Right.

00:37:42.230 --> 00:37:44.950
Then, by the way, there's
no hearing either.

00:37:44.950 --> 00:37:48.160
The cause of the ear couldn't be there

00:37:48.160 --> 00:37:50.330
and the result of the ear, hearing,

00:37:50.330 --> 00:37:51.870
couldn't be there either.

00:37:51.870 --> 00:37:54.140
The ear can't be there,
the chemicals in the ear

00:37:54.140 --> 00:37:56.620
can't be there, and the
function of the ear, hearing,

00:37:56.620 --> 00:37:57.940
can't be there. Why?

00:37:57.940 --> 00:37:59.730
Because you're looking at something.

00:37:59.730 --> 00:38:01.980
According to you, you're
looking at something.

00:38:01.980 --> 00:38:05.620
Something can be defined by
functioning at the moment,

00:38:05.620 --> 00:38:07.830
but it doesn't apply
to all the other senses

00:38:07.830 --> 00:38:08.663
at the same time,

00:38:08.663 --> 00:38:11.780
can not, according to this guy.

00:38:16.360 --> 00:38:19.500
I think we've got one more verse here.

00:38:19.500 --> 00:38:22.976
Did we lose everybody? Yeah!

00:38:22.976 --> 00:38:25.670
By the way, the 12th verse,

00:38:25.670 --> 00:38:29.800
which I think is the
final verse, right Tim?

00:38:29.800 --> 00:38:33.230
It's a summary. It's a summary
of the chapter. Thank God.

00:38:33.230 --> 00:38:35.440
At least if we understand the summary,

00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:37.660
we can say we know the chapter.

00:38:37.660 --> 00:38:39.837
So, let's look at the summary.

00:38:39.837 --> 00:38:41.228
,GANG ZHIG LTA LA SOGS PA YI,

00:38:41.228 --> 00:38:46.211
,SNGA ROL DA LTA PHYI NA MED,

00:38:47.636 --> 00:38:49.446
,DE LA YOD DO MED DO ZHES,

00:38:49.446 --> 00:38:52.262
,RTOG PA DAG NI LDOG PAR 'GYUR,

00:38:52.262 --> 00:38:54.820
And I like this image
because I like ice cream,

00:38:54.820 --> 00:38:58.137
but I never get it because
my wife doesn't let me

00:38:58.137 --> 00:39:01.910
Oh, I'm not... We've got three choices.

00:39:01.910 --> 00:39:04.420
Don't quote me.

00:39:04.420 --> 00:39:06.020
You've got three kinds of ice cream?

00:39:06.020 --> 00:39:07.233
Yeah, okay.

00:39:10.860 --> 00:39:13.070
Look, this is a summary of the chapter.

00:39:13.070 --> 00:39:16.870
If you understand the next
two minutes, you're okay.

00:39:16.870 --> 00:39:19.633
And I think you will. So no pressure.

00:39:21.041 --> 00:39:23.209
There's three kinds of ice cream here.

00:39:23.209 --> 00:39:24.850
You've got to choose
between the peppermint,

00:39:24.850 --> 00:39:26.300
the lemon, and the chocolate.

00:39:27.380 --> 00:39:29.103
Makes me want to choose one.

00:39:30.890 --> 00:39:34.390
So there's three different ideas

00:39:34.390 --> 00:39:35.370
in this whole chapter,

00:39:35.370 --> 00:39:39.338
and Nagarjuna kindly is
wrapping it up for us.

00:39:39.338 --> 00:39:41.260
He said, look, there's three ideas.

00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:43.800
If you get these three, don't worry about

00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:47.090
what you didn't understand, all right?

00:39:47.090 --> 00:39:49.265
What are these three?

00:39:54.150 --> 00:39:57.883
Can a seer exist before
they see? Yes or no?

00:39:59.240 --> 00:40:00.790
Can you call someone an astronomer

00:40:00.790 --> 00:40:02.630
until they look at the stars?

00:40:02.630 --> 00:40:04.793
No, cannot. So that's okay. Why?

00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:06.593
%BDAG BYA

00:40:06.593 --> 00:40:09.760
There's no appellation cause.

00:40:09.760 --> 00:40:11.670
There's nothing to call...

00:40:11.670 --> 00:40:13.470
there's no reason to
call them an astronomer

00:40:13.470 --> 00:40:15.010
until they look at the stars.

00:40:15.010 --> 00:40:17.230
So that's okay, we're
okay with that, right?

00:40:17.230 --> 00:40:18.920
You have to look at the stars

00:40:18.920 --> 00:40:20.910
before we can call you an astronomer.

00:40:20.910 --> 00:40:23.720
You have to say the mantras

00:40:23.720 --> 00:40:26.840
before we can call you a
Medicine Buddha practitioner.

00:40:26.840 --> 00:40:29.140
Something like that.

00:40:33.110 --> 00:40:36.273
Now the tricky one.

00:40:37.380 --> 00:40:39.450
When the girl's looking at the stars,

00:40:39.450 --> 00:40:40.490
is she an astronomer?

00:40:40.490 --> 00:40:43.070
In the moment that she's
looking at the stars,

00:40:43.070 --> 00:40:44.143
is she an astronomer?

00:40:48.370 --> 00:40:51.300
In the moment that the girl
is looking at the stars

00:40:51.300 --> 00:40:54.523
with her telescope, can
we call her an astronomer?

00:40:55.610 --> 00:40:57.280
Yeah, we just said that.

00:40:57.280 --> 00:40:58.570
After she looks at the stars,

00:40:58.570 --> 00:40:59.990
we can call her an astronomer.

00:40:59.990 --> 00:41:03.170
So in that moment that
she's looking at the stars,

00:41:03.170 --> 00:41:04.550
we can call her an astronomer.

00:41:04.550 --> 00:41:05.720
All right, good?

00:41:05.720 --> 00:41:08.830
Does she ever meet the stars?

00:41:08.830 --> 00:41:10.930
Does she ever have contact with the stars?

00:41:12.830 --> 00:41:14.670
An image of a star, does
she ever have contact

00:41:14.670 --> 00:41:16.940
with the image of a star?

00:41:16.940 --> 00:41:19.120
Is there a place in her life

00:41:19.120 --> 00:41:21.693
where a star overlaps with astronomer?

00:41:25.270 --> 00:41:28.480
Where being a star overlaps
with being an astronomer.

00:41:28.480 --> 00:41:32.860
I mean, she might be a star
astronomer, but... right?

00:41:32.860 --> 00:41:34.920
So I'll say it again.

00:41:34.920 --> 00:41:36.410
While she's looking at the stars,

00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:37.550
can you call her an astronomer?

00:41:37.550 --> 00:41:39.780
Yeah, I guess so.

00:41:39.780 --> 00:41:43.930
Does the astronomer and
the stars ever overlap?

00:41:43.930 --> 00:41:46.620
Is any part of her body a star?

00:41:46.620 --> 00:41:49.450
Is any part of the star an astronomer?

00:41:49.450 --> 00:41:52.662
Can we say they never overlap?

00:41:52.662 --> 00:41:56.437
Then in that case, she
can't look at the star.

00:41:58.400 --> 00:41:59.890
They never touch each other.

00:41:59.890 --> 00:42:04.890
She might also be swimming
in, what do you call it?

00:42:05.466 --> 00:42:08.750
Sayulita.

00:42:08.750 --> 00:42:10.300
Looking at the stars is swimming

00:42:10.300 --> 00:42:12.037
in Sayulita,

00:42:12.037 --> 00:42:13.290
because there's no reason
why she'd be astronomer

00:42:13.290 --> 00:42:14.630
because they never touch each other.

00:42:14.630 --> 00:42:17.890
She never makes contact with stars

00:42:17.890 --> 00:42:20.880
because they can't overlap.

00:42:20.880 --> 00:42:22.870
No part of her can become a star

00:42:22.870 --> 00:42:25.620
and no part of a star can become her.

00:42:25.620 --> 00:42:30.450
Therefore, they have to be
separate and disconnected.

00:42:30.450 --> 00:42:34.320
If they're disconnected,
then when she eats a banana,

00:42:34.320 --> 00:42:36.400
she's an astronomer.

00:42:36.400 --> 00:42:39.060
Because there's no more compelling reason

00:42:40.160 --> 00:42:42.620
that looking at the star
should make her an astronomer

00:42:42.620 --> 00:42:46.873
if it's not related to
astronomers, if they never overlap.

00:42:49.560 --> 00:42:51.060
Okay, third ice cream!

00:42:51.060 --> 00:42:52.870
You've got the first two ice creams?

00:42:52.870 --> 00:42:54.750
I'll repeat the two ice creams

00:42:54.750 --> 00:42:55.583
for you.

00:42:55.583 --> 00:42:57.760
Until she looks at the star,
she's not an astronomer.

00:42:57.760 --> 00:42:58.740
That's the first ice cream.

00:42:58.740 --> 00:43:01.660
Okay. I'm okay with that.

00:43:01.660 --> 00:43:03.843
While she's looking at the
star, she can't be an astronomer

00:43:03.843 --> 00:43:06.312
because the stars never touch her

00:43:06.312 --> 00:43:07.145
and she never touches the stars.

00:43:07.145 --> 00:43:08.970
If they never touch and she
can still be an astronomer,

00:43:08.970 --> 00:43:12.270
then when she's taking a
bath, she's an astronomer.

00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:15.900
Okay, third one.

00:43:15.900 --> 00:43:20.058
Is it after looking at the
stars that she's an astronomer?

00:43:21.263 --> 00:43:23.573
Does looking at the stars come first

00:43:23.573 --> 00:43:25.630
and then the astronomer is established

00:43:25.630 --> 00:43:28.500
by looking at the stars?

00:43:28.500 --> 00:43:30.750
Yeah! Well then she's also established

00:43:30.750 --> 00:43:33.170
by pizzas that fly to Mars

00:43:34.220 --> 00:43:37.310
because something that
doesn't exist anymore

00:43:37.310 --> 00:43:40.422
is making her an astronomer.

00:43:40.422 --> 00:43:41.860
The looking at the stars is done

00:43:41.860 --> 00:43:44.070
by the time you call her an astronomer,

00:43:44.070 --> 00:43:46.500
therefore, anything else
she ever could have done

00:43:46.500 --> 00:43:48.150
would also make her an astronomer,

00:43:48.150 --> 00:43:50.360
because there's no connection
between looking at the stars

00:43:50.360 --> 00:43:51.968
and becoming an astronomer,

00:43:51.968 --> 00:43:53.840
because they can't overlap either.

00:43:53.840 --> 00:43:56.890
In all three ice cream
cases, it's impossible.

00:43:56.890 --> 00:43:59.120
Something is fishy.

00:43:59.120 --> 00:44:01.483
This ice cream smells like fish.

00:44:02.530 --> 00:44:04.730
This particular ice
cream smells like fish.

00:44:04.730 --> 00:44:08.290
Each of those three choices is defective.

00:44:08.290 --> 00:44:10.433
Does the mantra cause the healing?

00:44:11.950 --> 00:44:14.010
So the mantra comes first.

00:44:14.010 --> 00:44:18.210
Or does saying the
mantra cause the healing

00:44:18.210 --> 00:44:20.017
and they're going on at the same time?

00:44:20.017 --> 00:44:23.380
Or do you have to heal somebody first

00:44:23.380 --> 00:44:24.697
and then you can call a mantra.

00:44:24.697 --> 00:44:26.680
Because if it doesn't heal anybody,

00:44:26.680 --> 00:44:28.180
it's not really a mantra.

00:44:28.180 --> 00:44:29.950
Which three?

00:44:29.950 --> 00:44:33.420
And Nagarjuna says none of the above.

00:44:33.420 --> 00:44:36.110
I'll say it again, let's
do it one more time.

00:44:36.110 --> 00:44:38.320
- Which came first? The
mantra or the healing?

00:44:38.320 --> 00:44:39.630
- Oh, mantra.

00:44:39.630 --> 00:44:42.703
- Okay, so if mantra
came before the healing,

00:44:42.703 --> 00:44:45.520
then the healing didn't
have a cause. - Why?

00:44:45.520 --> 00:44:49.694
- Because the mantra's gone
by the time you get healed.

00:44:49.694 --> 00:44:51.490
Then you've got a healing without a cause.

00:44:51.490 --> 00:44:53.300
- No, no, no, okay, the mantra goes on

00:44:53.300 --> 00:44:54.660
at the same time as the healing.

00:44:54.660 --> 00:44:58.741
- Okay, then the mantra also
causes rice to grow in Pluto.

00:44:58.741 --> 00:45:00.320
- Why?

00:45:00.320 --> 00:45:02.730
- Because they don't have any connection.

00:45:02.730 --> 00:45:05.200
There's no connection between the two.

00:45:05.200 --> 00:45:08.840
They can't connect, they cannot overlap.

00:45:08.840 --> 00:45:11.740
Saying the mantra and being
healed from the cancer

00:45:11.740 --> 00:45:13.970
are always different things.

00:45:13.970 --> 00:45:17.600
Saying a mantra is not
getting healed from cancer.

00:45:17.600 --> 00:45:20.090
It causes getting healed by cancer.

00:45:20.090 --> 00:45:22.460
Getting healed by cancer
comes after the mantra.

00:45:22.460 --> 00:45:24.550
They cannot go on at the same time.

00:45:24.550 --> 00:45:26.740
They're separate.

00:45:26.740 --> 00:45:29.500
It's not that 10% of healing is mantra

00:45:29.500 --> 00:45:31.930
and 10% of mantra is healing.

00:45:31.930 --> 00:45:35.300
Mantra comes first, and then it stops,

00:45:35.300 --> 00:45:36.133
and you get the healing.

00:45:36.133 --> 00:45:37.880
Okay, if it stops and
then you get the healing,

00:45:37.880 --> 00:45:39.980
then it can't be connected to the healing.

00:45:40.940 --> 00:45:42.857
There cannot be a relationship
between the mantra

00:45:42.857 --> 00:45:44.610
and the healing because the mantra stopped

00:45:44.610 --> 00:45:46.600
before the healing started.

00:45:46.600 --> 00:45:48.220
They never overlap.

00:45:48.220 --> 00:45:51.090
Then you could just, I don't
know, eat more croissants

00:45:51.090 --> 00:45:52.770
and it would heal cancer.

00:45:52.770 --> 00:45:56.105
That's my idea.

00:45:56.105 --> 00:45:57.950
And then the last possibility is,

00:45:57.950 --> 00:46:00.060
it's not a mantra until
somebody gets healed by it,

00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:02.070
then you can really call it a mantra.

00:46:02.070 --> 00:46:06.870
Okay. So after the mantra's
finished, it's a mantra, right?

00:46:06.870 --> 00:46:10.000
A mantra is not a mantra
until it finishes. Why?

00:46:10.000 --> 00:46:12.813
Because a mantra's not
a mantra until it heals.

00:46:13.950 --> 00:46:17.340
First comes the healing,
then the mantra is a mantra.

00:46:17.340 --> 00:46:20.520
Okay, so you don't have
to say the mantra. Why?

00:46:20.520 --> 00:46:22.337
Because by the time the healing comes,

00:46:22.337 --> 00:46:24.120
the mantra's gone anyway.

00:46:24.120 --> 00:46:25.550
You could have just eaten a pizza

00:46:25.550 --> 00:46:29.530
and it would have healed the cancer.

00:46:29.530 --> 00:46:32.030
None of the three connections
you think is going on

00:46:32.030 --> 00:46:36.070
between the mantra and the
healing the cancer is possible.

00:46:36.070 --> 00:46:38.040
There's something fishy.

00:46:38.040 --> 00:46:39.757
"Oh Geshe-la, just tell us what's going on

00:46:39.757 --> 00:46:41.440
and we won't worry about it."

00:46:41.440 --> 00:46:45.010
That's not Nagarjuna's style.

00:46:45.010 --> 00:46:46.850
He wants you to figure it out.

00:46:46.850 --> 00:46:50.650
Yay. Thank God because all the teachers

00:46:50.650 --> 00:46:51.950
who don't understand Nagarjuna

00:46:51.950 --> 00:46:55.222
really don't have to say
what they don't understand.

00:46:55.222 --> 00:46:58.526
You figure it out.

00:46:58.526 --> 00:47:00.300
No, we will figure it out.

00:47:00.300 --> 00:47:02.894
So, see you in the next class,

00:47:02.894 --> 00:47:05.087
on the emptiness of Medicine Buddha.

